<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">FRELIMO</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1962</span> · Also known as Mozambique Liberation Front, Frente de Libertação de Moçambique</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">FRELIMO, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> Liberation Front, was founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dar-es-salaam">Dar es Salaam</a> in June 1962 under Eduardo Mondlane by the union of exile nationalist groups. From bases in Tanzania it fought a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war against Portuguese rule from 1964 until Mozambique's independence in 1975, and it has governed Mozambique ever since, first as a Marxist-Leninist single party and from 1990 in a multi-party system.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frelimo.jpg" alt="FRELIMO" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archduke of Columbia · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_FRELIMO.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
